#40501
The Strange Forest~
Tall trees, covered in moss and black withered leaves, fill the landscape.
The strange uniformness of this forest, every tree standing in direct line 
to the ones next to it. So close they present themselves as a perfect wall 
of bark, moss and leaves. Each branch tightly woven in to the next trees 
branches, creating a canopy to block out any light. The forest looks planed,
or created, like a large painted square in the middle of a canvas of earth.
Paths seem to have been created by spaces where the trees did not grow or
where deliberately forgotten.
~
